// =============================================================================
// Chora Content Consumption — learner-owned Goal lifecycle events
// =============================================================================
//
// The Goal aggregate (ADR-204 §2, amends ADR-203) is the LEARNER-owned
// destination of the curious-first loop — it runs with ZERO Companions
// (ADR-204 Constraint-1). A Goal scopes a `concept_set`; the learner's
// verified progress is the share of that set they have MASTERED ("grown"
// Growth Edges, derived intra-domain — never stored on the Goal, see
// goal/progress.go). These two events make that progression OBSERVABLE +
// rewardable instead of a silent status flip — the Goal-level analogue of
// chora.consumption.weakness.grown.v1 (ADR-196), one tier up the aggregate
// hierarchy (an edge grows → a Goal's progress moves → at 100% it graduates).
//
// EMITTER: chora-consumption (the goal-graduation subscriber consumes
// weakness.grown.v1 and, per affected active Goal, recomputes the mastered
// share — emitting progress_updated below 100 % and graduated at 100 %).
//
// Domain placement: per the topic-domain-follows-the-affected-aggregate-root
// convention (see weakness.proto / creation/ai_assist.proto headers), BOTH
// events live in the `consumption` domain because the affected aggregate is the
// learner-owned Goal in chora_consumption.
//
// Aggregate root : goal (chora_consumption; learner-owned, ADR-204 §2)
// Owning domain  : Content Consumption (chora_consumption)
// Owning team    : Team 1 (Content)
// Topic prefix   : chora.consumption.goal.*
// Surface        : A+ (today-bar Goal %-ring + graduation celebration, CHO-1921)
//
// Subscribers (loosely-coupled, attach later):
//   - chora-sharing       — award the Three-Currency Economy on graduation.
//   - chora-consumption   — Companion reaction (the companion celebrates).
//   - chora-observability — engagement / D1 evidence.
// The A+ FE celebrates graduation by reading status='achieved' directly (it does
// NOT subscribe); these events drive cross-domain reward + live progress.
// =============================================================================

